# One table for UI translations

`AppLocale::trUi` reads a single `QHash<QString, UiTranslation>` (`english` + `spanish` per key). Adding a string means **one** new row. Do not keep parallel EN and ES hashes — keys diverge.

```cpp
// BAD — two tables; easy to add a key in only one language
return (language != Spanish) ? en.value(key, key) : es.value(key, key);

// GOOD — one struct per key; miss is explicit, then fall back to the key
struct UiTranslation { QString english; QString spanish; };
const auto iterator = table.constFind(key);
if (iterator == table.cend()) return key;
return language == Spanish ? iterator->spanish : iterator->english;
```

When you add `trUi("foo.bar")`, add `foo.bar` to `uiTranslationTable()` in `i18n/AppLocale.cpp` with both languages in the same initializer. Event tokens stay in `spanishEventMap()` (canonical English → Spanish).
